# Footnotes: the same note called from several places, here from cells of a table, with one number and one note.
Document (dev.stxt.pdf):
	Language: en
	Title: Footnotes · A note called twice
	Page:
		Paper: A5
		Margin: 15mm
	Styles:
		For element: Cell
			Typography:
				Markup: markdown
			Box:
				Padding: 3 6
				Border: 0 0 0.5 0
				Border color: rule
		For element: Header cell
			Typography:
				Bold: true
	Section:
		Text: Footnotes
			Style: topic
		Heading 1:
			Text: A note called twice
		Paragraph: A note can be called several times. All its calls carry the number of the first one, and the note goes once, at the bottom of the page of the first call. A cell with `Markup: markdown` can hold a call.
			Style: intro
		Table:
			Column sizes: * 30mm
